Warp Relay
Local Meta Global AI Developer Hackathon 2026 entry, started 2026-10-31.

This workspace integrates SentryWard, a pre-existing open-source project:
  https://github.com/gpu-verifier/sentryward
  Public revision: 421ff2c7d140341f64d2bc1f1edd045b65a7c403
  License: Apache License, Version 2.0
  Upstream author metadata: Zhihao Jia; see the repository for contributors.

The upstream source is fetched unmodified into vendor/sentryward. Its LICENSE
is preserved there and copied to licenses/SentryWard-Apache-2.0.txt. No
unpublished research worktree or private group code is included.

New work in this workspace: warp_relay/, gpu/, tests/, scripts/, docs/, and original
examples/neighbor_exchange microkernels and specifications. SentryWard's
verifier, public schema, prior research results and benchmark performance are
pre-existing contributions and are not claimed as new hackathon work.

API documentation used for the adapter:
  https://dev.meta.ai/docs/protocols/chat-completions
  Accessed 2026-10-31. No API credentials or model weights are bundled.

The real-case PTX snapshots are pre-existing public SentryWard corpus artifacts
mapped by their headers to PyTorch MultiMarginLoss.cu, WeightNorm.cu and
DeviceUtils.cuh at revision 2b3ec34829036a65cd9d1398ea72a0167dc37470.
They are not original Warp Relay kernels. WeightNorm's input configuration is
copied unchanged from the pinned public SentryWard example. Candidate PTX files
are derived from that public baseline by the recorded barrier deletions.
PyTorch copyright and redistribution terms are preserved in
licenses/PyTorch-LICENSE.txt. Its CUDA source was inspected at the pinned public
URL. Compiler reproducibility was not established. Limited numerical,
racecheck and timing measurements on a real B200 are recorded in
evidence/round4-20261031, with their fixed launch and testing boundaries.

The historical film's PageCam component is adapted from video-shotcraft:
  https://github.com/vincentwei1021/video-shotcraft
  Copyright 2026 Wei Yihao
  License: Apache License, Version 2.0
Its license is preserved in licenses/video-shotcraft-Apache-2.0.txt and the
modified source retains its origin and adaptation notice. No Gallery scene
implementation is included. Current film audio is separately licensed below.

The workbench UI uses Pierre Diffs 1.6.2 (Apache-2.0), Shiki and other lockfile-pinned open-source libraries. Full bundled dependency notices are retained in licenses/Pierre-Diffs-LICENSE.md and licenses/ui-third-party-notices.txt. The Linear reference image is not redistributed.

